## Freshness contract

- **Changing facts** (metrics, headcount, pricing, status) carry an as-of date on the page that states them, and name the system of record here.
- **Stable context** (methodology, frameworks, definitions) needs no as-of date — it's what the corpus is for.
- When a read fails, **say so on the page**. Never let an unlabelled stale number stand in for a current one; a downstream bot cannot tell the difference and will present it as current.

## Per-system notes

When a system is wired, write `wiki/sources/{tool}-api.md` capturing endpoints, auth flow, and the two or three queries actually used. Researched once, saved forever — and it keeps the next session from re-deriving it.
